<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Russo-Turkish War (1877–1878)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1877–1878</span> · Also known as Russo-Turkish War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Russo-Turkish War of 1877–1878 was fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, following uprisings among the Balkan Christian peoples. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s victory led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-san-stefano">Treaty of San Stefano</a> and then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-berlin">Congress of Berlin</a> in 1878, which recognised the independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, Montenegro and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>. The Ottoman Empire profile treats the war as a major step in the loss of Ottoman territory in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>.</p></div>
